p.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":null,"format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Which archetypes can reach which type","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":null,"format":"","indent":0,"type":"extended-heading","version":1,"tag":"h2"},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Your archetype constrains height and caps both attributes, so not every type is available to every archetype. Computed from the Pro Clubs Lobby catalog's own ranges:","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":null,"format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1},{"type":"html","version":1,"html":"<table>
<thead><tr><th>Archetype</th><th>Height</th><th>Agility</th><th>Strength</th><th>Best Explosive</th><th>Best Lengthy</th></tr></thead>
<tbody><tr><td>Shot Stopper</td><td>183–201cm</td><td>50–90</td><td>50–96</td><td>—</td><td>Lengthy</td></tr><tr><td>Sweeper Keeper</td><td>178–198cm</td><td>65–90</td><td>65–96</td><td>Mostly Explosive</td><td>Lengthy</td></tr><tr><td>Progressor</td><td>178–196cm</td><td>70–90</td><td>70–96</td><td>Mostly Explosive</td><td>Lengthy</td></tr><tr><td>Boss</td><td>180–196cm</td><td>65–90</td><td>75–99</td><td>Mostly Explosive</td><td>Lengthy</td></tr><tr><td>Engine</td><td>168–188cm</td><td>70–92</td><td>65–96</td><td>Explosive</td><td>Lengthy</td></tr><tr><td>Marauder</td><td>168–188cm</td><td>70–95</td><td>60–96</td><td>Explosive</td><td>Lengthy</td></tr><tr><td>Recycler</td><td>173–193cm</td><td>70–92</td><td>75–96</td><td>Mostly Explosive</td><td>Lengthy</td></tr><tr><td>Maestro</td><td>163–188cm</td><td>72–99</td><td>65–92</td><td>Explosive</td><td>Lengthy</td></tr><tr><td>Creator</td><td>163–188cm</td><td>72–99</td><td>65–92</td><td>Explosive</td><td>Lengthy</td></tr><tr><td>Spark</td><td>163–188cm</td><td>75–99</td><td>65–90</td><td>Explosive</td><td>Mostly Lengthy</td></tr><tr><td>Magician</td><td>163–188cm</td><td>72–99</td><td>65–90</td><td>Explosive</td><td>Mostly Lengthy</td></tr><tr><td>Finisher</td><td>165–191cm</td><td>72–99</td><td>70–92</td><td>Explosive</td><td>Lengthy</td></tr><tr><td>Target</td><td>178–196cm</td><td>70–92</td><td>75–99</td><td>Mostly Explosive</td><td>Lengthy</td></tr></tbody>
</table>","visibility":{"web":{"nonMember":true,"memberSegment":"status:free,status:-free"},"email":{"memberSegment":"status:free,status:-free"}}},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":1,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"7 of the 13 can reach full Explosive","type":"extended-text","version":1},{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":" — Engine, Marauder, Maestro, Creator, Spark, Magician and Finisher — all sharing a low minimum height with a high Agility ceiling. The 6 that cannot (Shot Stopper, Sweeper Keeper, Progressor, Boss, Recycler and Target) are blocked by height alone: their shortest legal build is still taller than the Explosive limit.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":null,"format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Full Lengthy is easier — only Spark and Magician cannot reach it, clearing the height bar but keeping a Strength ceiling too close to their Agility floor to open a 20-point gap. Every archetype can reach at least the Controlled Lengthy half-step.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":null,"format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Getting the type you want","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":null,"format":"","indent":0,"type":"extended-heading","version":1,"tag":"h2"},{"children":[{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":1,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Set height first.","type":"extended-text","version":1},{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":" It's the only input you can't change later, and it gates everything — above the Explosive height limit, you can never be Explosive regardless of attributes.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":null,"format":"","indent":0,"type":"listitem","version":1,"value":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":1,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Then protect the gap.","type":"extended-text","version":1},{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":" Chasing Explosive means treating Strength as something to leave alone.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":null,"format":"","indent":0,"type":"listitem","version":1,"value":2},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":1,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Re-check after every upgrade.","type":"extended-text","version":1},{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":" One point in the wrong attribute can flip you from Explosive to Mostly Explosive, silently.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":null,"format":"","indent":0,"type":"listitem","version":1,"value":3}],"direction":null,"format":"","indent":0,"type":"list","version":1,"listType":"number","start":1,"tag":"ol"},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Frequently asked questions","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":null,"format":"","indent":0,"type":"extended-heading","version":1,"tag":"h2"},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Does Pace affect AcceleRATE?","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":null,"format":"","indent":0,"type":"extended-heading","version":1,"tag":"h3"},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"No. Acceleration and Sprint Speed change how fast you end up going; they play no part in which profile you get. Only height, Agility and Strength do.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":null,"format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Is Explosive better than Lengthy?","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":null,"format":"","indent":0,"type":"extended-heading","version":1,"tag":"h3"},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Neither. Explosive wins the first few yards, suiting wingers and tight spaces. Lengthy wins longer runs, suiting centre-backs and strikers running in behind.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":null,"format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Can I change my acceleration type later?","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":null,"format":"","indent":0,"type":"extended-heading","version":1,"tag":"h3"},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"The attribute half, yes — the Agility/Strength gap moves as you spend points. Height is fixed at creation, so if height rules a type out, it's out permanently.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":null,"format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1}],"direction":null,"format":"","indent":0,"type":"root","version":1}}
